LAST-MODIFIED:20260803T140024Z
UID:52009-1787396400-1787410800@beachmetro.com
SUMMARY:Dutch Pot in Diaspora: A Black Art Salon & Liming
DESCRIPTION:The Black Art Salon will bring together visual art\, food-based storytelling\, community connection\, games\, and speed-friending. The gathering celebrates the creativity\, complexity\, memory\, resistance\, joy\, and future-building of Black communities across the African diaspora. \nThe exhibition centres and celebrates Black artists\, but friends\, neighbours\, and allies of all backgrounds are warmly invited to come lime with us. In Caribbean culture\, liming means hanging out\, relaxing\, and socializing with friends\, so pull up for art\, games\, conversation\, and community. \nThere is also current Call for Artists to submit their work to this exhibition\, and the deadline is Friday August 14th! Check out eastendarts.ca/artlabs2026 for more information.
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/dutch-pot-in-diaspora-a-black-art-salon-liming/
LOCATION:St. Matthew’s Clubhouse\, 450 Broadview Avenue\, Toronto\, M4K 2N3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://d28bcn7yu97icd.cloudfront.net/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/30115748/page-1.png
ORGANIZER;CN="East End Arts":MAILTO:info@eastendarts.ca
END:VEVENT
